   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 108 of the laws of 2016, amending the vehicle and\ntraffic law relating to authorizing a pilot residential parking permit system\nin the city of Buffalo, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9492",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9492-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 108 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9492\n\nSPONSOR: BASKIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 108 of the laws of 2016, amending the vehicle\nand traffic law relating to authorizing a pilot residential parking\npermit system in the city of Buffalo, in relation to extending the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe objective of this legislation is to allow the city of Buffalo to\ncontinue its residential parking permit system for an additional five\nyears.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends the effective date of chapter 108 of the laws of 201.6\nto provide for such chapter to remain effective until December 31, 2031.\n\nSection 2: provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 108 of the laws of 2016 authorized the city of Buffalo to adopt\na local law to implement a residential parking peituit program for the\nresidents of the Fruit Belt neighborhoods, which are adjacent to the\nBuffalo Niagara Medical Campus, to address the lack of available on\nstreet parking close to their homes that occurred because of the growth\nof the Medical Campus.\n\nThe pilot residential parking permit program has proven to be a success-\nful solution to the parking situation in the Fruit Belt since its imple-\nmentation in 2016. It is appropriate to extend the permit system, with\nthe same boundaries, for five additional years to provide the residents\nof the Fruit Belt, the city of Buffalo, and the occupants and visitors\nof the Medical Campus a stable and predictable parking permit program. A\nfive-year extension provides the opportunity for the Legislature to\nreview the residential parking permit parameters in the future.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
