    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 108 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9492A\n\nSPONSOR: BASKIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 108 of the laws of 2016, amending the vehicle\nand traffic law relating to authorizing a pilot residential parking\npermit system in the city of Buffalo, in relation to permanently author-\nizing such provisions\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to allow the city of Buffalo to\ncontinue its residential parking permit system.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the effective date of chapter 108 of the laws of 2016\nto remove the sunset of the law.\n\nSection 2 provides that this act shall be effective immediately.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION:\n\nThe amendments make the law permanent rather than a five-year extender.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 108 of the laws of 2016 authorized the city of Buffalo to adopt\na local law to implement a residential parking permit program for the\nresidents of the Fruit Belt neighborhoods, which are adjacent to the\nBuffalo Niagara Medical Campus, to address the lack of available on\nstreet parking close to their homes that occurred because of the growth\nof the Medical Campus.  The pilot residential parking permit program has\nproven to be a successful solution to the parking situation in the Fruit\nBelt since its implementation in 2016. It is appropriate to make this\nlaw permanent, with the same boundaries, to provide the residents of the\nFruit Belt, the city of Buffalo, and the occupants and visitors of the\nMedical Campus a stable and predictable parking permit program.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
